From de4822839fef7e6541a9fd88c83e9ea77e3b7668 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:01:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 215/294] gallium/pvr: the VS attribute shader compiles - the
 missing piece was pco_data, not SPIR-V

The handoff's next step was "build the VS from SPIR-V so the input carries the metadata pco's
PVFIO pass expects". That hypothesis was wrong, and the real cause is smaller: the driver passed a
zeroed pco_data into pco, so pco_nir_pvi() had no attrib_formats[] entry for the attribute location
and skipped it, and trans_load_input_vs() had no attribs[] range to name. The load was then never
lowered and the encoder produced a shader identical to a constant-position one. No SPIR-V detour is
needed; hand-built NIR works once the driver fills its half of the interface.

pvr_shader_init_vs_data() fills that half from the shader's declared inputs, the same two facts the
Vulkan driver fills from pipeline state (pvr_alloc_vs_attribs / pvr_init_vs_attribs).

One thing that looks like a bug but is not: pco_ra() forces hw_vtxins = 0 ("FIXME: Temporarily
disable vtxin allocation due to vec handling bug"), so the entry function's vtxins is 0 even when
the shader reads attributes - the loads address the vtxin registers directly. What the hardware
state needs is the driver-side range count, so pvr_shader.vtxins now carries
pco_data.common.vtxins and the probe requires 3 for its vec3 attribute.

Also completes the vertex fetch chain: pvr_shader_vertex_data() now patches the const map by entry
TYPE (the old walk advanced by one entry's size through a mixed list - it only worked by luck) and
patches the DOUTU_ADDRESS entry with the shader's USC offset, which is the instruction that
actually starts the VS after the fetch. Before this the attribute program ran and kicked nothing.

Verification (DRM noop shim, no GPU): probe exits 0, ALL PASS; VS reports vtxins=3; PDS data is
32 B with DOUTU -> 0x1000, the VS's USC offset; and the probe now requires the attribute VS binary
to differ from a constant-position VS, which is exactly the silent symptom that cost two rounds.

Next: the first draw needs the VDM state's VS half (vs_other_present with STATE3 code address,
STATE4 vtxouts, STATE5 sizes, STATE0 cam_size) and TA state, and the draw test must drop the
standalone VS launcher in favour of that chain. Those are first-draw work, not compiler work.
